From ce1b3bece63901c2a3fa5049bd6d8bdbd1b79acb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wai Chung <351198037+ternii-ai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:05:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] llama: 16 GB Mac defaults for the MoE expert cache (8
 experts, read-ahead, learned predictor)

On the SSD expert cache path (LLAMA_MOE_SSD=1) only:
- Qwen4Exp uses 8 routed experts per token instead of the model's 10. LLAMA_MOE_EXPERTS=N picks
  another supported count (1, 2, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10; an unsupported value warns and keeps the
  model's own), LLAMA_MOE_EXPERTS=0 keeps the model's own, and --override-kv always wins.
- Next-layer read-ahead: the experts of layer L+1 are predicted during layer L and read from the
  file while the GPU runs (LLAMA_MOE_PRED, LLAMA_MOE_PRED_K, default 6). A GPU keep-busy filler
  stops the GPU clocking down while it waits for the SSD (GGML_METAL_MOE_SPIN=0 turns it off).
- Learned predictor: <model>.trpw next to the model (first shard name without -0000N-of-0000M)
  is loaded automatically and replaces the next layer's router for read-ahead only; it changes
  which experts are read early, never the output. A missing or bad file falls back to the router
  with a warning. LLAMA_MOE_PRED_W=<file> loads a given file (errors are fatal);
  LLAMA_MOE_PRED_W= (empty) turns it off.
- The cache size gives back the extra attention KV of windows above 4096
  (LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_REF_CTX, 0 = off), so long windows stay within the GPU budget.
- Metal MUL_MAT_ID map0 kernel for 9 experts; separate row/simdgroup counts for the trit
  expert mat-vec.

Fully resident models and other back ends are unchanged.
---
